  m_Name: Equilibruim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonId: What is Equilibrium
  lessonTitle: What is Equilibrium
  lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
  popupDescription: Equilibrium occurs when the <b><#E09500>forces and moments acting
    on a structure are balanced</color></b>, allowing it to remain stable.
  almanacImage: {fileID: 0}
  lessonDescription: Structural equilibrium is the condition in which the <b><#E09500>combined
    forces and moments acting on a structure balance one another</color></b>. For
    a bridge to remain stationary and stable, loads such as its own weight and traffic
    must be <b><#E09500>balanced by reactions from its supports</color></b>. If these
    forces or moments become unbalanced, the structure may <b><#E09500>translate,
    rotate, or experience instability</color></b>.
